    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="95303712-9707-5cfc-9cfe-80d0d9aa7634" activityNameId="a8f7d862-0520-5559-9250-2a7afa92069e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 541aeaab-2868-48d7-a530-1c762adc5e23
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with vitrified clay pipe. DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Vitrified clay pipe, ID 300 mm, outer diameter 355 mm, wall thickness 27 mm, 56 kg/m, 2000 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_541aeaab-2868-48d7-a530-1c762adc5e23.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
